# Shop backups. Real customer and sales data — never commit these.
*.mpebak

# Stray personal files. This repository is on GitHub, and the working folder
# collects things that have nothing to do with the app — a scanned form, a
# screenshot sent over WhatsApp, an installer. None of them belong in the
# history, and `git add -A` would take every one.
#
# Matched by TYPE rather than by name on purpose: a .gitignore listing
# "GATE.pdf" and a dated WhatsApp image is itself a small disclosure, and it
# would only cover the strays that have already turned up. Nothing of these
# types is tracked -- the repository is source, PNGs under assets/, Markdown
# under docs/ and JSON config -- so these patterns cost nothing.
*.pdf
*.exe
*.msi
*.ppt
*.pptx
*.doc
*.docx
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.zip
*.rar
*.7z
